==English==

===Alternative forms===
* [[enquire]] {{qualifier|chiefly British}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{term/t|la|inquīrō||to seek for}}. Displaced {{etyl|enm|-}} {{term|enqueren|lang=enm}} (from {{etyl|fro|-}} {{term|enquerre|lang=fro}}, of the same source) and native {{etyl|ang|-}} {{term|speir||ask, inquire|lang=ang}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ɪnˈkwaɪɹ/}} {{a|UK}}
* {{audio|en-us-inquire.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|inquires|inquiring|inquired}} (''intransitive'' or ''transitive'')

# {{context|US|lang=en}} To [[ask]] (about something).
# To make an [[inquiry]] or an [[investigation]].

====Usage notes====
* In British English, the spelling '''[[enquire]]''' is more common, with '''inquire''' often reserved for official [[inquest]]s. In Canada and the US, both spellings are acceptable, though '''inquire''' is favored.

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|frain}}

